# Top-level inputs for the system-package venv. Release tooling
# (packaging/vendor-wheels.sh) resolves this on a networked host into the
# vendored, hash-locked manifest (requirements-lock.txt); the offline venv
# build (packaging/build-venv.sh) installs only from that manifest.
#
# Same pins as install.sh: mlx-lm goes in without its upstream mlx
# dependency (the wheel satisfies it), transformers carries the
# sentencepiece extra, and the resolver pins the transitive closure
# (huggingface-hub stays below 2.0 through transformers' own pin).
# The mlx-omarchy wheel itself is added from the release asset via
# --wheel. Voice extras (mlx-audio and friends) stay install.sh-only
# for the system package's first scope.

mlx-lm==0.31.3
transformers[sentencepiece]==5.16.1
numpy
protobuf
pyyaml
jinja2
huggingface_hub
